From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TR3600 port <local>
Date: Sat, 27 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_wed: apply MT7987 WED stability fixes

Port the MediaTek SDK MT7987 WED stability follow-ups to the Linux 6.18
hwpath backport. Also restore the mtk_wed_soc_data::wed_rev_id field that
the hwpath backport already references, without which the driver fails
to build.

- wed-13: disable/re-enable the PSE WDMA port across WiFi L1 SER
- wed-14: stop reporting TKID_WO_PYLD as a WED error status
- wed-16: initialize WDMA RX rings once and avoid double allocation
- wed-20: reduce the WED busy poll interval from 15 ms to 1 ms
- wed-21: reallocate the TX buffer pool after TX BM reset
- wed-23: derive TX BM packet counts from the WiFi token count

Not validated on hardware yet.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_wed.c
@@ -46,8 +46,8 @@
 #define MTK_WED_MIOD_ENTRY_CNT		128
 
 #define MTK_WED_TX_BM_DMA_SIZE		65536
-#define MTK_WED_TX_BM_PKT_CNT		32768
-#define MTK_WED_TX_BM_PKT_CNT_V3_1	17408
+#define MTK_WED_TX_BM_PKT_CNT(dev)		((dev)->wlan.nbuf * 2)
+#define MTK_WED_TX_BM_PKT_CNT_V3_1(dev)	((dev)->wlan.nbuf + 1024)
 
 static struct mtk_wed_hw *hw_list[3];
